The questions are about the state after all these actions.

=== Questions ===
- "fails": Does the kubectl command fail (exit with an error)? (yes = the command exits with an error; no = the command succeeds)
- "pods_terminated": Does the command cause any pod that was running before it to be terminated, deleted or evicted (within two minutes after the command)? (yes = at least one pod that was running before is terminated, deleted or evicted; no = every pod that was running before keeps running)
- "outage": Two minutes after the command, is there a Service that had ready endpoints before the command and now has no ready endpoints, or no longer exists? (yes = some Service that was serving now has no ready pod behind it, or is gone; no = every Service that was serving still has at least one ready pod behind it)
- "data_lost": Is data stored on a PersistentVolume permanently deleted (a volume is removed together with the files stored on it)? (yes = data stored on a persistent volume is permanently deleted; no = all data stored on persistent volumes is kept)
- "replicas_short": Two minutes after the command, does any Deployment or StatefulSet that still exists have fewer ready pods than its desired number of replicas? (yes = some Deployment or StatefulSet has fewer ready pods than it wants; no = every remaining Deployment and StatefulSet has all its replicas ready)
